==English==

===Etymology===
Probably euphemism for "this tit for that tit" made as simple and [[reduplicative]] as [[bric-a-brac]], [[pit-a-pat]], [[tic-tac]], [[zig-zag]], etc. <!-- {{rfe|date=May 2012}} -->

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[tit]] [[for]] [[tat]]}}

# {{idiomatic}} exactly [[equivalent]] return, [[retaliation]], [[retribution]]; [[an eye for an eye]].
#: ''If you hit me, I'll hit you back; '''tit for tat'''.''
# {{idiomatic}} roughly [[equivalent]] return of "this for that"; [[quid pro quo]].
# {{Cockney rhyming slang}} [[hat]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|exact return}} [[an eye for an eye]]
* {{sense|rough return}} [[quid pro quo]]

